==Battleground==
*Infinite [[Squire Rel]]s spawn, delay 3.33~13.33 seconds<sup>100f~400f</sup>.
*Infinite [[Pigeon de Sable]]s spawn after 13.33 seconds<sup>400f</sup>, delay 13.33~20 seconds<sup>400f~600f</sup>.
*Infinite [[Snache]]s spawn after 6.67 seconds<sup>200f</sup>, delay 6~13.33 seconds<sup>180f~400f</sup>.
*When the base reaches 99% HP:
**1 [[R.Ost]] spawns as the boss.
**10 [[Mooth]]s spawn, delay 6.67~16.67 seconds<sup>200f~500f</sup>.
**Infinite [[Pigeon de Sable]]s spawn, delay 5~10 seconds<sup>150f~300f</sup>.
**10 [[Pigeon de Sable]]s spawn, delay 0.67~2 seconds<sup>20f~60f</sup>.
**1 [[Kory]] spawns.

==Strategy==
The combination of Kory and R.Ost is deadly because you have to meatshield sparingly to prevent death by wave but must also have enough meatshielding to hold off R.Ost. The harder way to deal with it is to use two cheap meatshields ([[Crazed Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Manic Mohawk]], [[Cat (Normal Cat)|Mohawk Cat]]) as well as one strong meatshield ([[Crazed Tank Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Manic]] or [[Tank Cat (Normal Cat)|normal]] Eraser, whichever is stronger) along with [[Kotatsu Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Octopus Cat]] and ranged attackers like the [[True Form]]s of [[Ururun Wolf (Special Cat)|Ururun]] and [[Red Riding Mina (Special Cat)|Mina]]. [[Jagando Jr. (Special Cat)|Jagando Jr.]] works wonder here, being [[Strong Against|Strong against]] Traitless with his already powerful stats. He can absolutely obliterate the R.Ost.

However, there are some much easier strategies involving Uber Rare Cats:
*Any of the ranged wave-blockers ([[EVA Unit-00 (Uber Rare Cat)|EVA-00]], [[Hatsune Miku: MM2020 Tokyo (Uber Rare Cat)|Tokyo Miku]]) are great, as they allow you to meatshield normally without fear of Kory destroying everything.
*Certain [[:Category:Cats with Wave Immunity|Wave Immune]] units such as [[Togeluga (Uber Rare Cat)|Shishilan Pasalan]] also help in case Kory releases a Wave Attack.
*As expected, [[EPICFEST (Gacha Event)|EPICFEST]] exclusives destroy the stage.

